From 3f1201e7ed96c3102fa20f988ea6fff54cb34e5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spindle interop <spindle@tuna-os.invalid>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 23:29:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Dial named peers directly, sign federation requests, and
 fetch a named peer's keys

A node whose sidecar rides a datagram link can only address node ids;
a peer known by name (a venue gateway's upstream homeserver) is now
dialled over HTTP directly. Every outbound request carries a real
X-Matrix signature under ed25519:1 when the deployment signs, so a
Matrix peer can authenticate it against /_matrix/key/v2/server. Inbound,
a key resolver wraps the medium's and fetches a named peer's key
document, checking its self-signature. The lb ingress forwards
/_matrix/key/ so peers can fetch this node's document over the
federation port.
